file the Certificate of Amendment with Delaware.

.why = this legally changes your authorized shares and effectuates the reverse split.

---

## fees

⛔ **do NOT quote a total from this table without a re-check.** every row below
is from Delaware's published schedule, **revised 2026-08-01** — and a fee
schedule moves. re-read it before you pay:
[corpfiles.delaware.gov/Fee_Schedule/AugustFee2026.pdf](https://corpfiles.delaware.gov/Fee_Schedule/AugustFee2026.pdf)
(reachable from the hub at [corp.delaware.gov/fee](https://corp.delaware.gov/fee/)).

| item | cost | schedule row |
|------|------|--------------|
| Certificate of Amendment | **$214.00** ⚠️ *varies with stock* | `Amendment *$214.00` |
| each additional page | +$9.00 | county recording, per the schedule note |
| certified copy (each) | +$50.00 | column 2 |
| expedited — same day | +$200.00 | column 3 |
| expedited — 24 hour | +$100.00 | column 4 |
| expedited — 2 hour (Priority 2) | +$500.00 | schedule footer |
| expedited — 1 hour (Priority 1) | +$1000.00 | schedule footer |

⚠️ **the asterisk decides the answer on THIS stone specifically.** the schedule
marks the amendment fee `*VARIES BASED ON STOCK`, and its note says the column-one
amount holds "for a 1 page document, however, **may vary if stock changes**".
a share-count amendment is by definition a stock change — so **$214.00 is a
floor, not a quote**. call (302) 739-3073 for the figure on your own submission.

> 🚨 **this table read `$50` for the amendment and `+$100` for same-day.**
> both were wrong: the fee is **$214.00** (4.3×), and same-day is **$200.00**.
> the `$50` traced to a block quote attributed to `corp.delaware.gov/howtoform/`
> — a page that contains **neither** the word "amendment" **nor** "minimum fee".
> see `howto.reduce-franchise-tax-for-delaware-corp-solofounder.md`.
>
> ⭐ a stone is the worst possible home for an unsourced figure: a brief is
> *read*, a stone is **executed**. this one told an agent to record a
> `fee paid` against a number off by a factor of four.

