## timeline

⚠️ this table asks for a **duration**. do not put a cost in it — the costs are
in the fees table above, and a prior version of this stone carried three of them
here (one of which contradicted its own fees table).

| option | duration |
|--------|----------|
| standard (Priority 7 — Reg. Work) | ⛔ **none is published** — call for the current processed date |
| expedited — 24 hour | next business day |
| expedited — same day | same business day |
| expedited — 2 hour (Priority 2) | 2 hours |
| expedited — 1 hour (Priority 1) | 1 hour |

⛔ **the standard row has no duration because the Division publishes none.** the
four expedite tiers each carry a time; regular work carries a price of `$0` and a
sentence that declines to name an interval:

> "Processing time for **regular (non-expedited) work varies based upon the
> volume of items received** by our office."
>
> — the FAQ, `registrator/briefs/incorporation/variant=c-corp/refs/pulledAt=2026-09-25.de-faq-regular-work-turnaround.txt`

⇒ the substitute is a call, and the question has a shape: ask **"what date are you
currently at?"**, never **"how long will mine take?"** the first is on a clerk's
screen; the second is the forecast the FAQ declines to print.

⭐ an item already in the regular queue can still be **upgraded** to an expedite
tier by a call, so the cheap default is also the safe first move here.

> 🚨 **this row said `2-3 weeks` until 2026-09-25, with no hedge whatever.** the
> peer defect in `corp.franchise.reinstate/templates/4.file.revival.stone` at
> least carried an *"unsourced — treat it as an estimate"* caveat; this one
> presented an invented interval as a published fact.
>
> ⚠️ and note which file the cure reached first. the revival stone was corrected
> in the same pass that pulled the FAQ; **this stone is a different route, and a
> sweep for the FIGURE is what found it** — a sweep for the revival topic would
> have missed it entirely.

